# FreeLinX/ports - sysutils/pfetch : upstream source reference.
#
# UPSTREAM SOURCE: pfetch (Dylan Araps), MIT license. A system information
# tool written entirely in POSIX sh -- no compilation, no dependencies
# beyond a POSIX shell and standard utilities FreeLinX has already ported
# (uname, cat, etc). Chosen over fastfetch (a C/CMake project with dynamic
# optional dependencies) as a better fit for FreeLinX's minimal, BSD-style
# philosophy: nothing to compile, nothing to statically link, and it works
# directly with the already-ported netbsd-sh.
#
# github.com/dylanaraps/pfetch is ARCHIVED (read-only, no longer accepting
# changes), which means its `master` branch is permanently frozen -- pinning
# to it here is equivalent to pinning a commit SHA, since it can never move.
